##### slither
slither: 342 finding(s); gate at informational and above
  accepted  1 x [high] arbitrary-send-erc20: The `from` of safeTransferFrom is the immutable LP_VAULT_SWAP, not a caller-chosen address, and deposit reverts NotLPVaultSwap unless msg.sender == LP_VAULT_SWAP (REQ-ESCROW-002), so the escrow only ever pulls from the caller itself, the exact amount that caller approved for this call (REQ-ESCROW-003, REQ-SWAP-076). No third party's allowance can be spent. Covered by TEST-179 (depositOnlyFromLpVaultSwap fuzz), PROP-037 (Halmos, Certora).
  accepted  5 x [high] uninitialized-state: False positive of the per-contract analysis: proxyMarket, indebtedCount and marketRecords are declared in the abstract CollateralizationBase and written by other facets of the one deployed contract (pledge writes proxyMarket and marketRecords, markIndebted writes indebtedCount); the abstract facet Slither analyzes alone (DebtMark, Views, Ledger) does not contain the writer. In the deployed Collateralization every variable has its writer. Covered by TEST-010, TEST-272, TEST-269.
  accepted  8 x [medium] reentrancy-no-eth: Collateralization's external calls go only to the market's registered immutable LPVault, the factory-validated vault token, the Aave Hub and Spoke, and in pledge and recredit the RiskModule's view check and the market's LPOracle poke, always while a Lock member holds the Lock; every LPVault value move requires the Lock and Collateralization as caller, and every Collateralization state change requires the Lock held by its named caller, so no call can re-enter (REQ-VAULT-086, REQ-LOCK-010). The writes after a call are the ones 2.3 orders after it: the credit is read only after custody (REQ-VAULT-012) and pending amounts are booked from the balance delta measured around the unwind (REQ-VAULT-135). Covered by TEST-060, TEST-010, TEST-150, TEST-151, PROP-037 (Halmos).
  accepted  5 x [medium] unused-return: The ignored values are not needed and using them would be wrong: marketOf's shape is the LPVault's to enforce (Collateralization needs pool, poolId and tokens only); returnPosition's depositor is the LPVault's own record; topUpPosition's report is superseded by the live units read next (REQ-COLL-037); poke's price state is read by the RiskModule itself (Q-199); releaseToDepositor's report is replaced by the depositor's measured balance deltas (REQ-VAULT-088). Each call reverts on failure. Covered by TEST-238, TEST-237, TEST-018.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Route accounting is by balance deltas over the swap call, never by an external contract's return value: inRecv, each leg's output and every residue are rises of the route's own balances, and the output is LPVaultSwap's balance rise in TOKEN_OUT (REQ-ROUTE-008, REQ-ROUTE-009, REQ-ROUTE-014, REQ-ROUTE-015). The pool's returned (amount0, amount1) are not needed: the callback pays at most the hop's amount, once, only to the stored pool (REQ-ROUTE-013), and the hop's output is measured by _runHops as the route's balance rise. Trusting the returned deltas would be weaker than the measurement. Covered by TEST-232, TEST-177 and the callback tests of the DexPathRoute and WrapperThenDexRoute unit suites, PROP-068.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Only observationCardinality of slot0 is compared with twapMinObservations (REQ-PSTORE-027); price, tick and index are not used.
  accepted  3 x [medium] unused-return: Route accounting is by balance deltas over the swap call, never by an external contract's return value: inRecv, each leg's output and every residue are rises of the route's own balances, and the output is LPVaultSwap's balance rise in TOKEN_OUT (REQ-ROUTE-008, REQ-ROUTE-009, REQ-ROUTE-014, REQ-ROUTE-015). The shares minted are the route's measured static-aToken rise; the GHO or USDC output is LPVaultSwap's measured rise (the module pays it directly), and unsold shares and DAI below one gem unit are measured residues returned to LPVaultSwap (REQ-ROUTE-011, REQ-ROUTE-012). The returned share count, (assetAmount, ghoBought) and daiInWad duplicate these measurements. Covered by the PegModuleRoute unit suite, TEST-232, PROP-068 and PROP-044.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Only the answer of latestRoundData is used: the raw-price bound (REQ-CONFIG-035) is a listing-time magnitude check, not a price read, so round id and timestamps are irrelevant; freshness is enforced by the LPOracle. Covered by TEST-139.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Route accounting is by balance deltas over the swap call, never by an external contract's return value: inRecv, each leg's output and every residue are rises of the route's own balances, and the output is LPVaultSwap's balance rise in TOKEN_OUT (REQ-ROUTE-008, REQ-ROUTE-009, REQ-ROUTE-014, REQ-ROUTE-015). The assets that redeem returns duplicate the route's measured rise of the underlying, which is what the hops spend; with a fee-on-transfer underlying the measurement is the correct amount and the return value would overstate it. Covered by the WrapperThenDexRoute unit suite, TEST-232, PROP-068.
  accepted  3 x [medium] unused-return: activePriceRoutes returns (primary, alternate, replaced); the two routes are already the ones in force, so the replaced slot carries nothing the caller needs (REQ-CONFIG-072).
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Only answer and startedAt of latestRoundData are part of the sequencer-feed check (REQ-PSTORE-023); roundId, updatedAt and answeredInRound are not.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Setters return nothing, so the delegatecall's return data is empty by construction; Address.functionDelegateCall already bubbles any revert.
  accepted  1 x [medium] unused-return: Route accounting is by balance deltas over the swap call, never by an external contract's return value: inRecv, each leg's output and every residue are rises of the route's own balances, and the output is LPVaultSwap's balance rise in TOKEN_OUT (REQ-ROUTE-008, REQ-ROUTE-009, REQ-ROUTE-014, REQ-ROUTE-015). The dy that exchange returns duplicates the measured rise of hop.tokenOut that _runHops uses as the next hop's amount; a pool that over-reports cannot inflate it. Every hop runs with min_dy = 0 by specification (REQ-ROUTE-009); the single minOut check on LPVaultSwap's rise catches value lost on any hop. Covered by TEST-232, TEST-227, PROP-068.
  accepted  22 x [low] calls-loop: View calls in loops over the MarketRegistry's Spokes, markets and debt reserves for the liveness re-check (REQ-PSTORE-021, setMaxFlashFeeBps raise) and the debt-reserve scan (REQ-PSTORE-016, REQ-CONFIG-050). STATICCALL only, at execution of a governance setter or in a view; a reverting callee makes the setter revert (fail closed) and the liveness view return false.
